WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.534
-Good evening.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.000
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.167
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.701
Former president Trump
testified yesterday

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:09.267
at his civil fraud trial

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:12.000
and spent nearly four hours
on the witness stand.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.534
But the judge
had to call it a day

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:16.334
before they could ask him
a third question.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:17.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:20.234
During his testimony yesterday,
former president Trump

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.834
pulled a piece of paper
out of his suit jacket

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.534
that he claimed
would clear his name,

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.601
but the judge would not
let him read it

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:29.467
'cause, as usual,
it was classified.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:31.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.634
That's right,
during his civil fraud trial,

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.834
Trump pulled a piece of paper
out of his suit jacket

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.567
and said it would
completely clear his name.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:38.667
Dude, you couldn't have
cleared your name

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:42.801
if you'd pulled out a neuralyzer
from "Men in Black."

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:45.634
What piece of paper
could possibly clear your name?

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:49.367
Was it a birth certificate
with a different name?

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.400
[ As Trump ] Your Honor,
this clears my name because,

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.334
as you can see,
my name is Reginald Periwinkle.

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:58.634
You've got the wrong guy.

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.734
[ Normal voice ] Ivanka Trump
is set to testify tomorrow

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:03.868
as part of the civil fraud trial
against former president Trump,

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.834
marking -- making it, excuse me,

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:08.133
the first thing she's been
invited to in New York

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:09.601
in eight years.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:10.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:14.567
Democrats -- Have her
over to your house.

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:15.634
Feel so bad about it.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.534
Democrats reportedly
have concerns

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:19.667
about President Biden's
reelection campaign

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.501
and are worried that
his political advisers

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:23.834
are ignoring warning signs
of sinking support.

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:28.400
Said Biden, "There's nothing
to worry about, right, Jill?

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.467
Jill?!"

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:33.167
Amid reports that he has
declined an invitation

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.601
to attend King Charles's
75th birthday party,

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.501
a spokesperson for Prince Harry

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:39.434
said that he never
received an invite,

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:42.701
or, more likely,
Meghan got the mail that day.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.133
Guys, let me tell you something.

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:50.634
I don't think either
of them get the mail.

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:53.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:55.934
Elon Musk's brain implant
company, Neuralink,

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.767
has announced that
it's looking for volunteers

00:01:57.767 --> 00:01:59.133
for human testing.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.968
Well, actually, what they said
was "fresh volunteers."

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.734
That's right,
Musk's brain implant company

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:09.434
has announced it's looking for
volunteers for human testing.

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:11.033
I don't think he should be
meddling with something

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.501
he doesn't really understand,
like humans.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.767
The co-work--
I love what he did with Twitter.

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.801
I'd love to get him
up in my brain.

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:21.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:25.100
Love to get him up there
to fiddle around.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.367
Now it's not called
the brain anymore.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.601
It's called B.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:30.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:33.067
The co-working space
company WeWork

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.501
filed yesterday for bankruptcy.

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:37.267
Wait a minute.
Again?

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:38.801
You already went
out of business.

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:40.467
I watched a whole miniseries

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:42.567
about how you went
out of business,

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:44.167
and you were still in business?

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:48.267
Oh, my God, Trump's going to win
again, isn't he?

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.234
According to a new study,
daily marijuana use

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:51.868
could increase the risk
of a heart attack.

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:54.667
And that's why I only
smoke it nightly.

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:56.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:00.601
Using my B.

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:05.000
The CDC announced yesterday
it will expand

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.067
its airport disease
surveillance program

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:08.834
to include
more than 30 pathogens.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:12.234
Cool. I think I know where
you can find 27 of them.

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:14.467
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:20.067
The makers --
You guys all got feet.

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:22.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:25.033
Everybody's like, "Oh, feet,
a human foot.

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:26.801
I would never."

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.534
The makers of M&amp;M's
have unveiled

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:30.400
a new holiday flavor,
Toasty Vanilla,

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.067
which features
white chocolate candies

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.033
coated in brown,
white, and vanilla shell.

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:36.267
It's the holiday treat
that will have everyone saying,

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.367
"Do you have any normal ones?"

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:44.601
And finally, according
to the latest numbers,

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:47.701
Taylor Swift's new album
"1989 (Taylor's Version)"

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:51.267
has sold 1.6 million units
in the U.S.,

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:54.801
and it's made her
almost 8 cents on Spotify.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:55.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:57.234
And that was the monologue,
everybody.

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:59.334
We're off and running.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:01.400
We got a great show
for you tonight.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:04.234
She hosts the Emmy-winning
"Rachel Maddow Show"

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:05.934
Monday nights on MSNBC,

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:09.968
and her book "Prequel: An
American Fight Against Fascism"

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:11.167
is a page-turner.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:12.467
It's out now.

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:14.901
The one and only Rachel Maddow
is back on the show.

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:17.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:18.868
He's a Grammy-winning musician,

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:21.601
front man of one of my all-time
favorite bands, Wilco.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:24.734
His book "World Within a Song:
Music That Changed My Life

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:26.868
and Life That Changed My Music"
is out now.

00:04:26.868 --> 00:04:29.400
Jeff Tweedy is back
and joining us.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.334
Very excited about that.

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:33.667
You guys, this summer,
I did a podcast

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.834
called "Strike Force Five"
with the other talk show hosts,

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:38.534
and when the topic of favorite
guest came up, I had one name.

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:39.534
She's here tonight.

00:04:39.534 --> 00:04:40.767
You can catch her on tour now,

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:43.033
and also her new show,
"Ms. Pat Settles It,"

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:44.100
is everything you want it to be.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.701
Ms. Pat is back, everybody.

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:48.667
Quite the show.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:51.601
Speaking of
the great Jeff Tweedy,

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:54.000
he was also kind enough
to record a jingle

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.501
for the podcast I'm doing
with my brother,

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.067
"Family Trips with
the Meyers Brothers."

00:04:57.067 --> 00:04:58.968
We talk to people about
the trips they took

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:01.300
when they were kids,
the trips they're taking now.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.167
This week, just released today,
the great Nick Offerman.

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:08.968
So do check out "Family Trips"
wherever you get your podcasts.

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:11.067
Moving on,
we here at "Late Night"

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:15.033
don't always have enough time
to cover all of the recent news.

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:16.801
So here with a recap
is one of our writers,

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:20.234
Amber Ruffin, in a segment
we call "Amber Says What."

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:23.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.267
-Hey.

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:27.634
You guys,
things have been crazy.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.067
Okay, first of all,

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:32.968
I heard 80-year-old actor
Robert De Niro just had a child,

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.534
and I was like, "What?"

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:39.000
Then I heard 83-year-old
Al Pacino also just had a child,

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.534
and I was like, "What?"

00:05:40.534 --> 00:05:44.167
What old man is going
to have a toddler next, Seth?

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:46.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:49.834
-I do have a toddler.
-Gross. How?

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:51.400
-The normal way.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.334
-Ew!

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:54.934
-Why don't you have a child?

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:56.801
-Because I am a child.

00:05:56.801 --> 00:05:58.701
A sexy little child.

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:00.400
[ Tink! ]

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:03.334
Then I heard that
they arrested Tupac's killer,

00:06:03.334 --> 00:06:07.000
and I was like, "What...
is next on your to-do list?

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.400
Get a warrant
for John Wilkes Booth?"

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.968
You're late!

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:13.667
Why not figure out
who shot J.R.?

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.868
-Oh, it was Kristin Shepard.

00:06:15.868 --> 00:06:18.033
-You are so old.

00:06:18.033 --> 00:06:21.167
-I'm only five years
older than you.

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:23.567
-I don't like this anymore.

00:06:23.567 --> 00:06:27.300
Then I heard that Ron DeSantis
wears secret high-heeled boots,

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.701
and I was like, "Wh-ha-ha-at?"

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:34.334
You must hate being short more
than you hate drag queens.

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:36.868
Speaking of drag queens,
with those high heels,

00:06:36.868 --> 00:06:38.200
you are one sew-in away

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.701
from violating
your own anti-trans bill, honey.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:45.567
Then I read that all of
Trump's kids are testifying,

00:06:45.567 --> 00:06:47.801
and I was like, "What?!"

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:51.033
Ivanka, Don Jr., Eric.

00:06:52.868 --> 00:06:55.033
All the kids.

00:06:55.033 --> 00:06:57.734
Man, I think
he might go to jail.

00:06:57.734 --> 00:07:00.501
Now, I know, I know,
he may be rich,

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:03.334
he may be old,
and he may be a white man,

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:06.234
but -- oops, never mind,
he will never go to jail.

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:09.234
He'll probably just do what all
the other old guys are doing --

00:07:09.234 --> 00:07:14.234
have a baby, which I believe
to be a prison in its own right.

00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:16.534
Okay, so then I heard En Vogue

00:07:16.534 --> 00:07:20.067
is going to be in the
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:23.200
I was like, "What?!"
And I have to say this.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:26.067
Please, NBC, corporate daddy,

00:07:26.067 --> 00:07:29.367
you have to let me in
to see that.

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:32.701
Oh, Seth, do you have tickets
to the parade?

00:07:32.701 --> 00:07:33.801
-No.

00:07:33.801 --> 00:07:36.133
-Then what is the point of you?

00:07:36.133 --> 00:07:37.634
Why are we doing this?

00:07:37.634 --> 00:07:39.367
What is any of this for

00:07:39.367 --> 00:07:42.267
if it's not going to help us
see En Vogue?

00:07:42.267 --> 00:07:44.767
Then Britney Spears
released her memoir,

00:07:44.767 --> 00:07:48.000
"The Woman in Me," and spilled
the tea on Justin Timberlake.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.033
And I was like, "Wh-ha-aaaat?"

00:07:50.033 --> 00:07:51.501
It's, like, a lot,

00:07:51.501 --> 00:07:54.334
and I don't know if I'm allowed
to talk about what she said,

00:07:54.334 --> 00:07:56.767
but let's just say this.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.601
Now, do you want to hear
some more gossip?

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:09.367
Okay, so,
Congressman George Santos

00:08:09.367 --> 00:08:12.701
was running around his job
with a baby,

00:08:12.701 --> 00:08:14.501
and I was like, "What?"

00:08:14.501 --> 00:08:19.634
When asked if the baby was his,
he said, "Not yet."

00:08:19.634 --> 00:08:22.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.033 --> 00:08:26.434
Which brings us to a segment
called "Amber Says Why."

00:08:26.434 --> 00:08:29.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:34.534
Now, George Santos said
this baby wasn't his yet.

00:08:34.534 --> 00:08:39.167
Why? Yet? Is that a threat?
And if so, to who?

00:08:39.167 --> 00:08:40.968
To me? America?

00:08:40.968 --> 00:08:43.601
Whoever's baby that is?
What?

00:08:43.601 --> 00:08:46.200
Whose baby is that and why?

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:47.901
Why the baby, George?

00:08:47.901 --> 00:08:49.801
Why did they give
their baby to you?

00:08:49.801 --> 00:08:52.334
Did you trick somebody
and steal their baby?

00:08:52.334 --> 00:08:53.734
Where did you get
that baby from?

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:56.934
Does it want to go back?
Did you ever give the baby back?

00:08:56.934 --> 00:09:00.100
Why the baby, George?
For what reason?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.501
What purpose was the baby
supposed to serve?

00:09:02.501 --> 00:09:04.434
And did it serve that purpose?

00:09:04.434 --> 00:09:07.434
And why does that baby
look more qualified

00:09:07.434 --> 00:09:09.968
to work in Congress than you?

00:09:09.968 --> 00:09:11.934
This has been "Amber Says Why."

00:09:11.934 --> 00:09:14.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:15.601 --> 00:09:19.033
Then I read that Beyoncé's
"Renaissance" tour

00:09:19.033 --> 00:09:22.267
made $579 million.

00:09:22.267 --> 00:09:23.467
[ Audience cheers ]

00:09:23.467 --> 00:09:24.567
Me too, man.

00:09:24.567 --> 00:09:26.000
It made so much money,

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.367
it literally boosted the economy
everywhere it went.

00:09:29.367 --> 00:09:32.267
I read that and I was like...

00:09:32.267 --> 00:09:35.601
because I'm not about to mess up
the Beyoncé mute challenge.

00:09:35.601 --> 00:09:36.868
Mnh-mnh.

00:09:36.868 --> 00:09:39.000
Then I saw that Beyoncé
went to the premiere

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:42.834
of Taylor Swift's new movie,
and I was like, "What?!"

00:09:42.834 --> 00:09:45.367
Beyoncé is not at
a Taylor Swift premiere.

00:09:45.367 --> 00:09:49.300
A Taylor Swift premiere
is at a Beyoncé.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:51.167
And I can't even imagine

00:09:51.167 --> 00:09:53.400
what Beyoncé in a movie theater
looks like.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.534
Walking up to
the concession stand like,

00:09:55.534 --> 00:09:59.834
"I will have the Sugar Babies
and a bottle of Cristal."

00:09:59.834 --> 00:10:01.200
Then...

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.300
[ Laughter ]

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:06.734
It came out so much worse.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:11.100
Then I heard there were
a million bedbugs in Paris,

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:13.367
and I was like, "Quoi?"

00:10:13.367 --> 00:10:17.701
Then I found out Usher was doing
the Super Bowl halftime show,

00:10:17.701 --> 00:10:19.834
and I was like, "What!"

00:10:19.834 --> 00:10:22.434
Well, I guess I'm going to
have to cook him

00:10:22.434 --> 00:10:25.434
a real big breakfast
that morning.

00:10:25.434 --> 00:10:26.901
Not because
I'm sleeping with him,

00:10:26.901 --> 00:10:30.000
but because I had to take on
an extra job as Usher's cook

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.100
'cause the writers' strike
lasted five months.

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:35.200
Then I found out the actors
were still striking,

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.367
and I was like, "What?"

00:10:37.367 --> 00:10:38.901
Matter of fact, Seth,

00:10:38.901 --> 00:10:41.467
how am I allowed to be
doing this right now?

00:10:41.467 --> 00:10:44.000
-Well, late-night television
shows fall under a specific --

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.467
-Ohh! Shut up.

00:10:46.467 --> 00:10:49.934
Then I heard that genetic
testing company 23andMe

00:10:49.934 --> 00:10:53.200
was hacked, and I was like,
"What...were you thinking

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.167
when you gave away all
your genetic information

00:10:55.167 --> 00:10:56.701
to some random company?"

00:10:56.701 --> 00:10:59.634
See, that's why
I never did 23andMe.

00:10:59.634 --> 00:11:02.367
Well, that and in case
I ever want to do a murder.

00:11:02.367 --> 00:11:04.567
I want to get away with it.

00:11:04.567 --> 00:11:06.834
Then I heard
Congresswoman Lauren Boebert

00:11:06.834 --> 00:11:08.868
got kicked out
of the musical "Beetlejuice"

00:11:08.868 --> 00:11:10.901
for getting felt up by some guy.

00:11:10.901 --> 00:11:12.801
And I was like, "What?!"

00:11:12.801 --> 00:11:15.467
"Beetlejuice"?
More like "Some Like It Hot."

00:11:18.234 --> 00:11:21.234
"Some Like It Hot,"
co-written by Amber Ruffin,

00:11:21.234 --> 00:11:23.834
now on Broadway
at the Shubert Theatre.

00:11:23.834 --> 00:11:26.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:26.868 --> 00:11:30.367
Boebert, why would you guys
stay in your seats for that?

00:11:30.367 --> 00:11:32.000
At least escape to the bathroom

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.901
and pretend
you're taking a whiz.

00:11:33.901 --> 00:11:36.968
"The Wiz,"
written by Amber Ruffin,

00:11:36.968 --> 00:11:40.167
touring America and coming
to Broadway March 29th.

00:11:40.167 --> 00:11:42.534
Tickets available
at wizmusical.com.

00:11:42.534 --> 00:11:44.834
-Hey, Amber, why do you
keep interrupting this bit

00:11:44.834 --> 00:11:46.501
to plug all
your Broadway musicals?

00:11:46.501 --> 00:11:49.067
-Because the strike
took too long,

00:11:49.067 --> 00:11:51.901
and I got to make money
to take care of this baby.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.734
-Amber, is that your baby?

00:11:58.734 --> 00:12:00.701
-Not yet.
[ Tink! ]

00:12:00.701 --> 00:12:02.501
This has been "Amber Says What."

00:12:02.501 --> 00:12:04.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:08.701 --> 00:12:09.834
-Amber Ruffin, everybody.

00:12:09.834 --> 00:12:12.133
We'll be right back
with Rachel Maddow.

